sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, DECISIONS R1-R4, rule 22 (official cfgmgmt, no shipped script). docs/reference/node-provisioning.md#orbit-cli.
  %% Real steps 2026-11-02: prepare, node-N (fleet-release-node: gate, cli, record), finish.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · POST /api/v1/fleet/cli/converge
  %% kind: fleet.cli_converge
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Target Node<br/>reached over ssh
  Note over GW: Converge the CLI<br/>task #5170
  %%> When:
  %%> - an operator or a tool calls `POST /api/v1/fleet/cli/converge`, for the CLI-eligible Nodes of the rollout set
  %%> Input:
  %%> - optional API field `node_ids`, for example `[12]`, limits convergence to those eligible Nodes
  %%> - without it, the whole rollout set is selected; an ineligible listed Node is rejected before admission
  %%> What it decides:
  %%> - per Node: the CLI release with its SHA-256, the root profile, and the public SSH descriptor of each Node that installs
  %%> - a Node without a CLI caller is skipped (`cli_not_required`); a Node whose release is unpublished is also skipped; neither needs an SSH target
  %%> Result:
  %%> - task #5170 recorded with the full intent; the Gateway replies 202
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-fleet-cli-converge
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209) for the selected Nodes
  Note over SW: Freeze the Node list<br/>prepare
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - reads the admitted intent once and records the Nodes in order
  loop each Node, one at a time
    Note over SW: Check the Node may publish<br/>fleet-release-node · gate
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - the `fleet-release-node` child starts on Node 209; its `gate` step checks that every earlier Node succeeded and the task is not cancelled
    %%> - a skipped Node or a planning error records the outcome without touching the Node
    SW->>N: Install the CLI release<br/>cli · node-cli-install
    %%> How:
    %%> - Swamp reaches Node 12 over SSH from 209, with `@swamp/ssh` and the admitted host keys
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - reads `orbit --version`; a Node that runs this release, a newer one, or a commit build keeps it
    %%> - otherwise downloads the release with `@swamp/cfgmgmt/fetch` and its `checksum`, checks the new file reports the release version, and switches the link with `@swamp/cfgmgmt/link`
    %%> - a file that does not report a valid Orbit version is replaced by the admitted release
    %%> - writes root's profile, 0600, with `@swamp/cfgmgmt/file`
    Note over SW: Record the CLI outcome<br/>record
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - the `record` step on Node 209 records `converged` or `unchanged` with the CLI version, or `cli.install_failed`
    %%> Not included:
    %%> - the Node agent; its `observer` step runs only for `fleet.rollout`, so this task needs no worker on Node 12
  end
  Note over SW: Report each Node<br/>finish
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - reads each Node's `record` output and returns one bounded result per Node
  alt every Node converged
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event · per Node
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Record each Node<br/>task done
    %%> Result:
    %%> - task #5170 succeeds; `operation:show` returns each Node's outcome and CLI version
  else a Node fails
    N--xSW: install or check failed
    %%> When:
    %%> - a download, checksum, version check, link or profile write fails on Node 12
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>Node 12 · cli.install_failed
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - Swamp visits no later Node; later Nodes stay `pending`
    Note over GW: Fail the task<br/>Node 12 · task failed
    %%> On the Node:
    %%> - the old CLI link stays when the switch did not happen; there is no rollback
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - fix the cause and call converge again; it is a new task and safe to rerun
  end
